&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Your personal data will be retained by Baringa for up to two years, in accordance with our &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.baringa.com/globalassets/careers/dp-007-nerpn-amer--apac-recruitment-privacy-notice-word.pdf&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Notice (AMER &amp;amp; APAC)&lt;/a&gt;, to assess your application and meet applicable reporting and legal obligations. In line with the Australian Privacy Act and Singapore’s Personal Data Protection Act (PDPA), you may have rights to access, correct, or request limited deletion of your personal data. For more information, please contact us at &lt;a ----------<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(0, 53, 142); font-family: helvetica, arial, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;About Baringa&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Baringa is a global consulting firm that partners with leaders to drive change and create value. With deep industry expertise, and enabled by advanced technology, the firm helps clients to deliver with greater confidence and certainty. With over 2,000 people across the UK, Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, the firm combines global insight with local understanding.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The firm works across energy and resources, financial services, government and public sector, consumer products and retail, pharmaceuticals and life sciences, manufacturing, and technology, media and telecoms, with capabilities spanning strategy, transformation and operational excellence – all powered by advanced technology, data, AI and digital innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Clients value Baringa’s collaborative approach and the way its teams integrate seamlessly – all working with a shared understanding of what matters most. The firm is known for its kind, curious experts who listen closely and care deeply about client success as they help clients transform energy markets, modernise financial platforms, expand telecoms and digital networks through advanced data analytics, enable digital services in government, and unlock growth in consumer sectors.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Certified as a&amp;nbsp;&lt;em&gt;Great Place to Work &lt;/em&gt;around the world, Baringa has been recognised by the &lt;em&gt;Financial Times &lt;/em&gt;in 22 categories of its UK Leading Management Consultants rankings, and by &lt;em&gt;Forbes &lt;/em&gt;for four consecutive years as one of the World’s Best Management Consulting Firms.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #00358e; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;&quot;&gt;Our Graduate Analyst Programme&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Graduate Analyst role offers the opportunity to start and grow your career at Baringa. As a permanent member of our team from day one, you&#39;ll work on a variety of real client and internal projects, develop valuable skills, and make a meaningful contribution from the outset.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work alongside experienced consultants, building both your technical and professional capabilities through structured learning, hands-on experience, and ongoing development opportunities. Along the way, you&#39;ll build relationships across the business, collaborate with colleagues from different teams and sectors, and contribute to work that makes a real impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re a recent graduate looking to kick-start your career, Baringa offers a supportive and collaborative environment where you can develop your skills, gain practical experience, and build a successful long-term future with us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re looking for &lt;strong&gt;Graduate Analysts&lt;/strong&gt; to join our &lt;strong&gt;Energy &amp;amp; Resources&lt;/strong&gt; practice, with opportunities available across several of our specialist business units. During the application process, you&#39;ll have the opportunity to select the business unit that best aligns with your interests and aspirations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The business units currently hiring are:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Commodities Energy &amp;amp; Trading&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;Our commodities and energy trading focused team operates across all major commodity and energy companies in Europe, the US and Singapore. From metals traders and miners, through oil majors, freight and shipping specialists to power and gas traders. Our people bring deep industry expertise to help our clients translate strategy into action, to enter new markets, build new trading capabilities, and to revolutionize their IT landscapes. &lt;br&gt;&lt;br&gt;&quot;From day one I have worked directly with clients on their complex trading transformation journeys. This has involved face-to-face engagement with our internationally based clients, visiting client site within weeks of starting at Baringa.&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Desired skills: Problem solving, IT interest, data skills, interest in commodity markets, personable and confident on client site&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Desired Degrees: &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;Engineering, Economics, Data science&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Energy Products&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We turn Baringa&#39;s deep energy market expertise into trusted data, insights and software products that our clients rely on as they navigate the energy transition. Our team create the market simulations and forecasts used by investors, developers, and utilities around the world to support strategic decision-making. We combine experts covering energy markets, data science, software development, and economics to create digestible data-led insight to our clients. Depending on your background you could be working with either our market research, modelling, or communications teams&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Desired Skills: &lt;/em&gt;&lt;em&gt;A keen interest in energy markets, comfortable handling large datasets and extracting insight for a wide audience, clear presentation and storytelling ability, programming (e.g. Python, SQL), using AI (for coding, for agentic workflows), experience using numerical models/simulation, interpersonal skills.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Desired Degrees: STEM subjects, Economics, Operational Research&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Markets &amp;amp; Transactions&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We help investors, developers, utilities, lenders and corporates make well-informed commercial decisions across the energy transition. We combine deep expertise in energy markets and infrastructure with strong commercial and transaction advisory capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our work ranges from market fundamentals analysis, power price forecasting and asset optimisation through to commercial strategy, M&amp;amp;A transactions, financing processes and investment due diligence. We work on some of the energy sector&#39;s most complex and high-profile challenges, helping clients deploy capital, manage risk and unlock value in rapidly evolving markets.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Successful candidates will combine analytical rigour and curiosity with a strong commercial mindset, and an interest in understanding how energy markets, investment decisions and business strategy intersect.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Desired Skills: Commercial acumen and strategic thinking, Quantitative analysis, modelling and data interpretation, Structured problem-solving and critical thinking, Energy market and energy systems knowledge, financial analysis and investment appraisal, Strong communication, stakeholder management and interpersonal skills, Ability to synthesise complex information into clear recommendations&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Desired Degrees: Economics, Engineering, Mathematics, Physics, Finance, Business / Management, Data Science, Statistics or Operational Research, Other quantitative disciplines.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Economics, Policy, Regulation, and Commercial&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We support clients from policy development to implementation, from regulatory strategies to business case submissions, and from competition cases to expert opinion. Our economists, policy specialists, regulatory experts and techno-economic modellers work alongside governments, regulators, investors and corporates - shaping the frameworks and decisions that underpin multi-billion-pound investment across energy, utilities and wider infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Desired Skills: Economic and quantitative analysis, written communication, structured problem-solving, policy &amp;amp; regulatory awareness, interpersonal skills.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Desired Degrees: Economics, Public Policy, Politics/PPE, Econometrics, Statistics, Finance&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;u&gt;Transition, Assets and Infrastructure&lt;/u&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our Transition, Assets &amp;amp; Infrastructure team helps energy, utilities and infrastructure organisations deliver complex transformation across the full asset asset lifecycle&amp;nbsp; from&amp;nbsp; capital programmes, asset management, operate and maintain and decommissioning.&amp;nbsp; We work with clients to develop their asset strategy, improve the performance of critical infrastructure, deliver large-scale capital investments, shape future operating models, and unlock value through technology, data and AI. Combining expertise in engineering, project delivery, operations, technology and business transformation, we help clients solve complex challenges and deliver lasting outcomes across asset-intensive industries.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Desired Skills: Problem Solving, Curiosity &amp;amp; Learning Mindset, Strong Communication Skills, Analytical &amp;amp; Structured Thinking, Interest in Energy, Infrastructure and Technology&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Desired Degrees: STEM including engineering disciplines, Data Science,&amp;nbsp; etc.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #00358e;&quot;&gt;So, what&#39;s in it for you?&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You’ll join with a cohort of our Graduate Analysts. As a cohort, you will participate in our Analyst Development Programme. Our programme is designed to develop the client, commercial and people skills that you need for a successful career at Baringa.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You will join our Global Analyst Community, connecting Analysts with one another to share their experiences and lessons learnt, whilst also gaining knowledge and skills from experienced Baringa people&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You decide on the development you need. We invest in you, to ensure you remain the best in the business, through formal training and qualifications, coaching and mentoring.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;You can talk to anyone in the business. There are no barriers, and everyone is accessible, from our Analysts to our Partners. Out Partner to consultant ratio of 1:10, means you get to learn and work alongside our Directors and Partners on a daily basis.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We’re proud to put people first with wellbeing at the forefront of our culture, one example of this is that every employee receives £300 a year to put towards their wellbeing!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;All employees participate in the Baringa Group Profit Share Scheme, which seeks to ensure that everyone has a stake in the success of the company.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;We recognise everyone needs a well-deserved break - As such we have introduced the ‘Re-charge’ benefit meaning Baringa will offer all employees an additional 2 weeks of paid leave after 5 years continuous service.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lastly, we recognise the importance of work-life balance and we know that the ‘ideal’ balance will vary from person to person and will change at different stages of our working lives.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: #00358e;&quot;&gt;Requirements:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
